  "title": "Vowel signs review: family words",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "You can now read most of Unit 3's family words on your own: **মামা, মামি, খালা, খালু, চাচা, চাচি, দাদা, দাদি, নানা, নানি, ফুফু**.\n\n**Reading routine**: (1) find each consonant; (2) look left, right, below and around it for a sign; (3) say consonant + vowel; (4) a consonant with no sign keeps its `o`, which is often silent at the end of a word.\n\n**Same sound, different spelling**: ি/ী and ু/ূ. **Wrap-around**: ো/ৌ. Next: conjuncts, where two consonants stack with no vowel between them (শিক্ষক, ধন্যবাদ).",
